	(text "R604 (0.05 Ohm) causes a 50 mV/A drop: USB5 is about 4.95 V at 1 A. Feedback\nis before the shunt. U601 is a 1 A IC with internal current, short-circuit\nand thermal protection. D601 indicates rail presence; R604 does not set the\ncurrent limit."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 141 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.55 1.55)
				(thickness 0.15)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
